      <h2 class="display">
        A reading community,
        <em>but not really.</em>
      </h2>

      <p>
        The whole point is the Sunday. The actual reading, under a tree, eight to ten in the morning. It's free, has been since we started, will keep being. Everything else we do — bookmarks, brunch, group photos, the occasional brand we like — happens around that.
      </p>

      <p>
        Pune's one chapter. Bombay runs theirs on Saturdays and Sundays both because the crowd's bigger. Bengaluru has its own thing. Jaipur too. A couple more cities are starting up. Name's shared. The rest is local.
      </p>

